1
00:01:38,110 --> 00:01:43,970
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:46,789
[Episode 6]

3
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:00,430
Chen.

4
00:02:00,430 --> 00:02:01,710
Does your brother have a girlfriend?

5
00:02:01,710 --> 00:02:02,430
My brother?

6
00:02:02,430 --> 00:02:03,310
I don't think so. Why?

7
00:02:03,310 --> 00:02:03,920
Perfect!

8
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:05,480
I've got my eye on him.

9
00:02:06,380 --> 00:02:09,289
[Non-Smoking Ward]

10
00:02:10,870 --> 00:02:11,560
Where is he?

11
00:02:12,630 --> 00:02:13,310
Right here.

12
00:02:16,190 --> 00:02:17,030
So, you heard

13
00:02:17,030 --> 00:02:18,230
what I just said, huh?

14
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:20,560
What do you think?

15
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:22,000
Give me a straight answer.

16
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:23,680
Chen, are you serious?

17
00:02:23,710 --> 00:02:24,870
Why wouldn't I be?

18
00:02:25,030 --> 00:02:25,710
W-What

19
00:02:25,870 --> 00:02:27,240
do you see in him?

20
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:33,140
I think you're good enough for me.

21
00:02:36,030 --> 00:02:37,079
Why don't we give it a shot?

22
00:02:37,079 --> 00:02:37,940
What do you say?

23
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:43,120
I don't think you're good enough for me.

24
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:44,050
What did you say?

25
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:45,400
You heard me.

26
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:46,980
Say that again.

27
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:53,280
I said

28
00:02:53,710 --> 00:02:54,800
we're not right for each other.

29
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:56,400
No, that's not what you said.

30
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,150
You said

31
00:02:58,870 --> 00:03:00,470
I wasn't good enough for you.

32
00:03:00,870 --> 00:03:01,590
I'm off to work.

33
00:03:01,590 --> 00:03:02,560
Get back here!

34
00:03:06,470 --> 00:03:08,710
You think I'm being nice to you,
so you can walk all over me?

35
00:03:08,710 --> 00:03:10,240
I give you a couple of compliments,
and suddenly

36
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:11,680
you're all high and mighty?

37
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:13,680
You think you can get away with this?

38
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:16,000
Getting all cocky, huh?

39
00:03:18,079 --> 00:03:19,560
You think I can't find a man?

40
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:21,960
It's not like I'm begging you
for anything!

41
00:03:22,590 --> 00:03:23,430
What,

42
00:03:24,079 --> 00:03:25,150
do you have eight kidneys or something?

43
00:03:25,150 --> 00:03:27,120
Why should I have
to chase after you, huh?

44
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:27,910
Huh, man?

45
00:03:28,910 --> 00:03:29,960
Listen,

46
00:03:30,430 --> 00:03:31,280
I'm not even gonna

47
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:32,540
bother with you today.

48
00:03:34,710 --> 00:03:35,770
I'm giving you time

49
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:38,050
to go ask around and find out

50
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:39,960
what people around this area think of me.

51
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:40,750
Got it?

52
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:45,860
You barbarian.

53
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:50,740
[Vending Machine]

54
00:03:47,079 --> 00:03:48,340
You've got some nerve!

55
00:03:57,430 --> 00:03:58,960
Am I not good enough for him?

56
00:03:59,310 --> 00:04:00,470
He's not good enough for you.

57
00:04:00,470 --> 00:04:00,960
He is.

58
00:04:02,470 --> 00:04:03,150
Get over here.

59
00:04:03,150 --> 00:04:04,080
D-Don't hit me!

60
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:05,190
If you do,
I'll just lie down on the ground!

61
00:04:05,190 --> 00:04:06,430
Get over here!

62
00:04:07,470 --> 00:04:08,270
Get over here!

63
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:25,270
Let's get started.

64
00:04:25,270 --> 00:04:25,720
Okay.

65
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:32,190
Perform a lumbar puncture
to measure the opening pressure

66
00:04:32,190 --> 00:04:34,750
and collect cerebrospinal fluid
for analysis.

67
00:04:34,750 --> 00:04:35,390
Doctor,

68
00:04:36,159 --> 00:04:37,890
what's wrong with my daughter?

69
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:41,680
She was fine when we left.

70
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,190
The patient has a high fever

71
00:04:43,190 --> 00:04:44,390
and nuchal rigidity.

72
00:04:45,159 --> 00:04:46,760
An intracranial infection?

73
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:49,159
Let's wait for the test results.

74
00:04:49,310 --> 00:04:49,920
Doctor,

75
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:51,800
money's not an issue.

76
00:04:52,070 --> 00:04:53,950
Give my daughter the best medication.

77
00:04:53,950 --> 00:04:55,480
Don't worry about the money just yet.

78
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:56,480
If an intracranial infection

79
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:57,510
is confirmed,

80
00:04:57,630 --> 00:04:58,480
she'll need

81
00:04:58,480 --> 00:05:01,010
antibiotics classified as restricted-use.

82
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:06,430
We're out of money.

83
00:05:06,430 --> 00:05:07,360
Will you shut up?

84
00:05:08,510 --> 00:05:10,510
I'll go borrow some money right now.

85
00:05:12,630 --> 00:05:14,920
They might not be able
to borrow any money.

86
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:16,270
There's no time to worry about money.

87
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:19,080
[Nurses' Station]

88
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:17,760
We need to save her first.

89
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:24,330
You go first.

90
00:05:25,190 --> 00:05:25,800
Hello.

91
00:05:25,950 --> 00:05:26,510
Hello.

92
00:05:26,510 --> 00:05:27,510
Is Dr. Yang Ran here?

93
00:05:27,510 --> 00:05:28,430
He's next door.

94
00:05:28,430 --> 00:05:28,950
Thank you.

95
00:05:28,950 --> 00:05:29,880
You're welcome.

96
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:36,450
Working that hard, huh?

97
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:38,100
Director Chen,

98
00:05:38,310 --> 00:05:39,070
what brings you here?

99
00:05:39,070 --> 00:05:40,270
Just came to see you.

100
00:05:42,190 --> 00:05:43,159
I heard your hospital

101
00:05:43,159 --> 00:05:44,430
has a new doctor,

102
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:45,530
Liu Zhengliang,

103
00:05:45,950 --> 00:05:47,680
who performed a major surgery.

104
00:05:47,830 --> 00:05:49,560
Let me see the medical records.

105
00:05:50,830 --> 00:05:51,630
That won't do.

106
00:05:51,630 --> 00:05:52,870
I'm afraid that wouldn't be appropriate.

107
00:05:52,870 --> 00:05:54,120
Why not?

108
00:05:54,510 --> 00:05:55,750
We're sister hospitals,

109
00:05:55,750 --> 00:05:56,750
and I'm an expert.

110
00:05:58,360 --> 00:05:59,480
The hospital has its rules.

111
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:01,280
Can't I learn something from it?

112
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:03,480
Forget it, forget it.

113
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:04,070
Pretend I never asked.

114
00:06:04,070 --> 00:06:04,390
Director Chen.

115
00:06:04,390 --> 00:06:05,720
What are you doing here?

116
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:06,870
Easy, easy.

117
00:06:06,870 --> 00:06:07,870
I'll take you there, all right?

118
00:06:07,870 --> 00:06:08,400
Let's go.

119
00:06:09,870 --> 00:06:11,800
Doctor, could you hurry things up?

120
00:06:12,270 --> 00:06:13,930
Any chance I could cut in line?

121
00:06:14,630 --> 00:06:15,920
No need. You're the only one here.

122
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:16,800
What line?

123
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:18,950
Sign here.

124
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:22,600
[Body Fluid Specimen Drop-Off]

125
00:06:23,870 --> 00:06:24,480
Just wait.

126
00:06:43,510 --> 00:06:44,720
If it were me,

127
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,130
I wouldn't dare pull a stunt like that.

128
00:06:48,830 --> 00:06:50,000
What a genius.

129
00:07:00,270 --> 00:07:03,630
What gives him the right
to turn my daughter down?

130
00:07:05,750 --> 00:07:07,920
Look at her! She's got tons

131
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:09,950
o-of guys chasing

132
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:12,190
after her around here.

133
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:14,330
Why not give it another try?

134
00:07:15,510 --> 00:07:17,510
It's not easy to find someone
you really like.

135
00:07:17,510 --> 00:07:18,710
I'm not trying again.

136
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:20,510
I won't settle for someone I like

137
00:07:20,510 --> 00:07:21,840
or someone who likes me.

138
00:07:22,390 --> 00:07:25,190
It has to be someone I love
and who loves me back.

139
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:26,650
No settling.

140
00:07:29,870 --> 00:07:30,680
I've gotten all my friends

141
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:31,870
from the winter fishing community

142
00:07:31,870 --> 00:07:32,800
to help search.

143
00:07:33,270 --> 00:07:34,390
Still nothing.

144
00:07:34,390 --> 00:07:35,070
We still haven't

145
00:07:35,070 --> 00:07:36,070
found your mom.

146
00:07:37,680 --> 00:07:38,390
It's okay.

147
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:40,420
You were right.

148
00:07:42,190 --> 00:07:43,510
No news is good news.

149
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:46,810
As long as there's hope,
that's good news.

150
00:08:08,110 --> 00:08:09,770
Her temperature's come down.

151
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:12,800
Run the tests again

152
00:08:13,310 --> 00:08:15,440
and check the protein and cell counts.

153
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:17,190
Um, Doctor...

154
00:08:17,190 --> 00:08:17,800
A cotton swab.

155
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:19,360
I-I mean, please give our Jiao

156
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:20,890
whatever the best medicine

157
00:08:21,070 --> 00:08:22,950
you have here is.

158
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:24,980
Money's no object.

159
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:26,510
You don't need to keep talking to me

160
00:08:26,510 --> 00:08:27,360
about money.

161
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:28,800
I'm a doctor.

162
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:30,070
My job is to treat patients.

163
00:08:30,070 --> 00:08:31,800
Money has nothing to do with it.

164
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:33,480
I'm sorry, Doctor.

165
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:35,559
I didn't mean anything by it.

166
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,200
Zhang Jiao's white blood cell count
has come down.

167
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:52,750
Other than the antibiotics,

168
00:08:52,750 --> 00:08:53,200
there really isn't much else

169
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:54,530
that'll cost them a lot.

170
00:08:55,270 --> 00:08:56,670
We're still short by 153.

171
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:58,320
We're short by 153, right?

172
00:08:58,760 --> 00:09:02,260
[Work-Related Injury
Registration and Billing]

173
00:08:59,120 --> 00:08:59,910
Look,

174
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:01,960
I've got 86 on this card,

175
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:04,120
and another 60-something.

176
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:05,440
I'll get you the rest tomorrow.

177
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:06,790
I'll go see what I can do right now,

178
00:09:06,790 --> 00:09:07,480
okay?

179
00:09:10,270 --> 00:09:11,480
I'll definitely have it by tomorrow.

180
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:13,140
We can't stop the medication.

181
00:10:13,150 --> 00:10:15,280
Why didn't you knock before coming in?

182
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:16,440
I did.

183
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:19,650
What do you need?

184
00:10:20,510 --> 00:10:21,840
Can we waive part

185
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:23,570
of Zhang Jiao's medical bills?

186
00:10:28,030 --> 00:10:28,630
No.

187
00:10:29,910 --> 00:10:31,000
Does Xiaoximen Hospital

188
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:31,960
have any

189
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:33,390
charitable assistance programs?

190
00:10:33,390 --> 00:10:34,550
Given our hospital's reputation,

191
00:10:34,550 --> 00:10:35,550
what do you think?

192
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:40,320
Here's the thing.

193
00:10:40,630 --> 00:10:41,630
Zhang Jiao's case

194
00:10:41,630 --> 00:10:42,910
is highly representative.

195
00:10:42,910 --> 00:10:44,120
If we can save her,

196
00:10:44,270 --> 00:10:45,440
I can't speak for the whole country,

197
00:10:45,440 --> 00:10:47,720
but it would certainly be
a rare case in the province.

198
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:48,790
It's worth publicizing

199
00:10:48,790 --> 00:10:51,190
and could help turn our reputation around.

200
00:10:51,750 --> 00:10:53,000
With that in mind,

201
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:55,210
is there room for negotiation?

202
00:11:03,670 --> 00:11:05,600
I don't care what your reasons are.

203
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:07,390
As long as you stay,

204
00:11:07,630 --> 00:11:08,360
we can talk.

205
00:11:09,600 --> 00:11:11,320
Those antibiotics are expensive.

206
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:12,200
If you leave

207
00:11:12,870 --> 00:11:14,960
and something unexpected happens to her,

208
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:16,510
all that money I've spent
will have gone to waste.

209
00:11:16,510 --> 00:11:18,000
You're a hospital president.

210
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,390
How can you think about
nothing but money?

211
00:11:19,390 --> 00:11:20,720
You're a doctor,

212
00:11:21,360 --> 00:11:22,270
yet you're here talking to me

213
00:11:22,270 --> 00:11:23,360
about money, too.

214
00:11:42,150 --> 00:11:43,010
How about this?

215
00:11:43,320 --> 00:11:44,200
I'll waive 40%

216
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:46,960
of her medical expenses,

217
00:11:47,720 --> 00:11:49,120
but you'll owe me a favor.

218
00:11:52,790 --> 00:11:53,390
Deal.

219
00:11:53,390 --> 00:11:55,120
But let me make one thing clear:

220
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:56,480
I'll leave as soon as she wakes up.

221
00:11:56,480 --> 00:11:57,870
Pleasure doing this with you.

222
00:11:57,870 --> 00:11:58,440
Wait,

223
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:02,900
let me show you something.

224
00:12:05,150 --> 00:12:05,680
Let's go.

225
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:11,470
[Laboratory Department] [Restroom]

226
00:12:11,470 --> 00:12:11,690
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

227
00:12:11,760 --> 00:12:14,400
[Biochemistry Laboratory]
[Laboratory]

228
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:13,050
President Long.

229
00:12:14,470 --> 00:12:15,510
[Immunology Laboratory]

230
00:12:21,870 --> 00:12:22,550
This way.

231
00:12:39,750 --> 00:12:41,410
Does this room look familiar?

232
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:46,510
It's yours now.

233
00:12:46,720 --> 00:12:47,720
If you live here instead of commuting,

234
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:49,200
you won't be affected by the snow,

235
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:50,270
whenever it falls.

236
00:13:42,870 --> 00:13:44,440
No need to thank me.

237
00:13:44,630 --> 00:13:46,440
I'm doing it to exploit you.

238
00:13:58,030 --> 00:13:58,600
You didn't

239
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:00,200
plan this all along, did you?

240
00:14:03,390 --> 00:14:06,250
How could I have planned
for that patient to show up?

241
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:09,080
Well,

242
00:14:09,080 --> 00:14:10,120
the president said

243
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:10,670
he could waive

244
00:14:10,670 --> 00:14:12,270
40% of the medical expenses.

245
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:13,750
For Zhang Jiao?

246
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,630
Did you went to see the president?

247
00:14:16,630 --> 00:14:18,160
How did you get him to agree?

248
00:14:18,670 --> 00:14:20,000
You can go

249
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:21,730
tell the patient's family now.

250
00:14:22,510 --> 00:14:24,080
Go on, take the credit.

251
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:26,940
If I tell them,
they'll feel like they owe me a favor.

252
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:28,550
I don't mind.

253
00:14:32,270 --> 00:14:32,870
So,

254
00:14:33,120 --> 00:14:34,870
um... are you still leaving?

255
00:14:42,510 --> 00:14:43,720
Not for now.

256
00:14:45,150 --> 00:14:46,720
Then go tell them. Go on.

257
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:49,670
He told you to go, so just go.

258
00:14:49,670 --> 00:14:51,480
Why are you acting all shy?

259
00:14:51,870 --> 00:14:53,400
What's it got to do with you?

260
00:14:56,750 --> 00:14:57,360
What,

261
00:14:58,320 --> 00:14:59,440
are we off work already?

262
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:00,120
No.

263
00:15:01,360 --> 00:15:03,120
Well, Dr. Liu said

264
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:04,320
he's not leaving for now.

265
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:05,240
He just talked to the president

266
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:07,200
and got Zhang Jiao's medical expenses

267
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:08,480
reduced by 40%.

268
00:15:09,270 --> 00:15:09,960
Really?

269
00:15:10,630 --> 00:15:12,230
That's great! That's great!

270
00:15:14,670 --> 00:15:15,360
All right, all right.

271
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:16,480
Dinner's on me tonight!

272
00:15:16,480 --> 00:15:17,610
Let's get together!

273
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:19,600
Seriously, Huang?

274
00:15:19,670 --> 00:15:21,150
I-I'm calling to confirm it.

275
00:15:21,150 --> 00:15:22,030
You're so generous!

276
00:15:22,030 --> 00:15:22,550
Let's celebrate

277
00:15:22,550 --> 00:15:23,630
Dr. Liu's

278
00:15:23,630 --> 00:15:25,270
return!

279
00:15:25,790 --> 00:15:26,600
Li,

280
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:26,910
Li,

281
00:15:26,910 --> 00:15:27,910
eserve that big private room

282
00:15:27,910 --> 00:15:28,600
for me tonight.

283
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:30,320
I don't like social gatherings.

284
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:31,270
I'm socially awkward.

285
00:15:31,270 --> 00:15:32,200
I'll pass.

286
00:15:32,670 --> 00:15:33,510
Wait a second.

287
00:15:35,240 --> 00:15:36,080
Come on, Dr. Liu.

288
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:37,000
Let's go.

289
00:15:37,240 --> 00:15:38,910
Our team hasn't had a dinner together yet.

290
00:15:38,910 --> 00:15:40,080
It'll be a great chance for everyone

291
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:40,840
to get to know each other.

292
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:42,120
Exactly!

293
00:15:42,120 --> 00:15:44,480
-Let's all get together and have some fun.
-I'm here to work,

294
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:46,080
not to build relationships.

295
00:15:52,150 --> 00:15:52,750
L-Li,

296
00:15:52,750 --> 00:15:54,000
I'll call you back.

297
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,510
Okay, okay.

298
00:15:56,600 --> 00:15:57,670
We're just happy

299
00:15:57,670 --> 00:15:58,800
for you, that's all.

300
00:15:59,510 --> 00:16:00,390
Fine, fine, fine.

301
00:16:00,390 --> 00:16:00,910
No worries,

302
00:16:00,910 --> 00:16:01,960
no pressure.

303
00:16:13,510 --> 00:16:15,110
The president, honestly...

304
00:16:15,790 --> 00:16:17,080
What's wrong, Huang?

305
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:19,270
Nothing. It's just that our president

306
00:16:19,270 --> 00:16:21,320
keeps using this trick,
and it works every time.

307
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:22,320
What trick?

308
00:16:22,630 --> 00:16:24,000
Isn't it the same thing

309
00:16:24,030 --> 00:16:25,480
he did with Dr. Liu?

310
00:16:25,550 --> 00:16:27,150
The same old trick. You know.

311
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:28,910
Remember last time, Mingming?

312
00:16:28,910 --> 00:16:30,030
Didn't you make him waive

313
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:31,240
the medical expenses

314
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:32,200
for that patient, too?

315
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,080
What was

316
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:34,500
that condition again?

317
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:39,270
The... the...

318
00:16:40,030 --> 00:16:41,790
spontaneous brain...
brain hemorrhage case,

319
00:16:41,790 --> 00:16:42,270
right?

320
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:43,630
I remember that one.

321
00:16:43,630 --> 00:16:45,240
She got played by the president.

322
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:46,000
Dr. Che,

323
00:16:47,240 --> 00:16:49,300
how did the president screw you over?

324
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:54,600
Hold on.

325
00:16:56,320 --> 00:16:57,960
We shouldn't talk
about the president here.

326
00:16:57,960 --> 00:16:58,550
It's not good.

327
00:16:58,550 --> 00:16:59,960
It's not the right place.

328
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:01,240
Honestly,

329
00:17:01,240 --> 00:17:02,550
when you're new here,

330
00:17:03,120 --> 00:17:04,200
you really should join us

331
00:17:04,200 --> 00:17:05,000
for more get-togethers.

332
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:05,440
Right.

333
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:06,880
You need to get
to know Xiaoximen Hospital better.

334
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:07,310
Right.

335
00:17:07,310 --> 00:17:08,640
Most importantly, you need to understand

336
00:17:08,640 --> 00:17:09,960
what kind of person
our president really is.

337
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:11,359
So how did things work out

338
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:13,099
between you and him in the end?

339
00:17:15,829 --> 00:17:16,790
No, not here.

340
00:17:16,790 --> 00:17:17,589
Not here.

341
00:17:17,589 --> 00:17:18,310
Let's talk about it at the restaurant.

342
00:17:18,310 --> 00:17:19,109
Let's talk about it at the restaurant.

343
00:17:19,109 --> 00:17:19,550
Come on, come on,

344
00:17:19,550 --> 00:17:21,920
-Let's talk about it at the restaurant.
-Let's go.

345
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:23,030
Why go so early?

346
00:17:23,349 --> 00:17:24,640
We'll be there for the first seating,

347
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:25,750
so the food will come out faster.

348
00:17:25,750 --> 00:17:26,510
Huang,

349
00:17:26,510 --> 00:17:28,240
you've thought of everything.

350
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:29,830
Come on,

351
00:17:29,830 --> 00:17:30,890
let's go! Let's go!

352
00:17:48,480 --> 00:17:49,200
Kang Sheng?

353
00:17:49,590 --> 00:17:50,110
Yeah.

354
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:52,730
Yang Ran.

355
00:17:54,030 --> 00:17:54,480
Huang.

356
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:56,340
Let's get together another time.

357
00:17:57,920 --> 00:17:58,640
Well...

358
00:17:59,350 --> 00:18:01,410
How long has your vision been blurry?

359
00:18:02,680 --> 00:18:03,960
About half a year.

360
00:18:04,440 --> 00:18:06,350
Everything looks blurry,

361
00:18:06,550 --> 00:18:08,810
like I'm looking through frosted glass.

362
00:18:10,550 --> 00:18:11,950
Let me check your pupils.

363
00:18:12,030 --> 00:18:14,480
Doctor, there's no need. Don't bother.

364
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,880
I had an MRI at No. 1 Hospital.

365
00:18:17,550 --> 00:18:19,480
They said I have a pituitary tumor.

366
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:22,310
The doctor said

367
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:25,270
it's best to have a family member
with me when I have brain surgery.

368
00:18:25,270 --> 00:18:26,270
The thing is,

369
00:18:27,310 --> 00:18:28,370
I can't find anyone

370
00:18:28,640 --> 00:18:29,500
to come with me.

371
00:18:31,350 --> 00:18:33,400
Doctor, please, help me out.

372
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:35,070
No, you...

373
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:37,400
You can't do this. Take your money back.

374
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:38,640
Let me do this. Let me.

375
00:18:39,480 --> 00:18:41,000
Zhong Yang. Zhong Yang!

376
00:18:41,750 --> 00:18:42,480
Buddy!

377
00:18:43,830 --> 00:18:44,550
Huang.

378
00:18:44,550 --> 00:18:45,110
Man,

379
00:18:45,110 --> 00:18:46,110
it's been ages since we all got together.

380
00:18:46,110 --> 00:18:46,790
I've missed you, you know?

381
00:18:46,790 --> 00:18:47,830
Yeah, yeah, I know, Huang.

382
00:18:47,830 --> 00:18:48,640
I'm starving.

383
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:51,510
You guys go ahead. I'm not coming.

384
00:18:51,510 --> 00:18:52,510
Come on, Dr. Liu.

385
00:18:52,510 --> 00:18:54,440
It's fine. They're colleagues
from other departments.

386
00:18:54,440 --> 00:18:55,200
Let me introduce you to everyone.

387
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:55,480
Everyone,

388
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:56,680
let me introduce

389
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:58,480
our department's new colleague,

390
00:18:58,480 --> 00:18:59,410
Liu Zhengliang.

391
00:18:59,510 --> 00:19:00,750
He's, uh...

392
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:01,720
he just got here.

393
00:19:01,720 --> 00:19:03,350
He's a little shy,

394
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:04,750
but this young man

395
00:19:04,750 --> 00:19:05,790
is really good at his job.

396
00:19:05,790 --> 00:19:07,590
People who are good at their jobs

397
00:19:07,590 --> 00:19:08,790
tend to be a little...

398
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:09,400
Yeah.

399
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:09,920
It's okay, buddy.

400
00:19:09,920 --> 00:19:11,000
I know you don't know anyone yet.

401
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:11,350
Come on

402
00:19:11,350 --> 00:19:12,400
and have dinner with us,

403
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:13,310
and you'll get to know everyone.

404
00:19:13,310 --> 00:19:13,830
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

405
00:19:13,830 --> 00:19:14,550
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

406
00:19:14,550 --> 00:19:15,610
Let's go together.

407
00:19:15,720 --> 00:19:16,440
Let's go.

408
00:19:16,830 --> 00:19:17,640
I'm thinking

409
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:20,030
of installing a row of cabinets here,

410
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:21,000
um...

411
00:19:21,030 --> 00:19:22,720
selling fresh flowers here,

412
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,730
putting funeral wreaths here,

413
00:19:25,070 --> 00:19:27,440
and stocking burial clothes
and funeral caskets here.

414
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:28,720
Then I'll put a sofa here

415
00:19:28,020 --> 00:19:31,460
[107 Xiaoximen Hospital]

416
00:19:28,720 --> 00:19:30,350
so I can take a nap during my lunch break.

417
00:19:30,350 --> 00:19:31,550
Oh he's off work now.

418
00:19:32,790 --> 00:19:33,960
Why the long face?

419
00:19:35,240 --> 00:19:36,270
He looks like someone bullied him.

420
00:19:36,270 --> 00:19:37,750
Dr. Zhong was like that
when he first got here, too.

421
00:19:37,750 --> 00:19:39,160
Right. W-Who isn't like that at first?

422
00:19:37,860 --> 00:19:40,420
[107 Xiaoximen Hospital]

423
00:19:39,160 --> 00:19:39,690
Exactly.

424
00:19:40,510 --> 00:19:41,840
He's got quite a temper.

425
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:48,440
So, how's that going now?

426
00:19:48,440 --> 00:19:49,160
It's okay.

427
00:19:49,160 --> 00:19:51,310
Who upset him?

428
00:19:51,480 --> 00:19:52,720
Why is he unhappy?

429
00:19:55,070 --> 00:19:55,640
Chen,

430
00:19:56,640 --> 00:19:57,590
how did I never realize

431
00:19:57,590 --> 00:19:59,520
you were such a hopeless romantic?

432
00:20:00,920 --> 00:20:02,920
You moved

433
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:03,920
our whole business

434
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:06,270
to Xiaoximen Hospital
just for that human beanpole.

435
00:20:06,270 --> 00:20:07,670
You looking for trouble?

436
00:20:08,510 --> 00:20:10,160
You think I'd really do all this

437
00:20:10,160 --> 00:20:11,240
for Wonder Doc?

438
00:20:12,030 --> 00:20:12,720
Couldn't dodge that one.

439
00:20:12,720 --> 00:20:14,120
This is a great location.

440
00:20:14,640 --> 00:20:17,200
I should grow the business
and make it stronger, right?

441
00:20:17,200 --> 00:20:18,640
Why don't you focus

442
00:20:18,640 --> 00:20:20,840
on improving the business first, okay?

443
00:20:21,070 --> 00:20:22,830
If you're going to get involved,
do it properly.

444
00:20:22,830 --> 00:20:24,830
Hey, hey, slow down! It's too runny!

445
00:20:25,440 --> 00:20:27,900
Honestly, you never know
your own strength.

446
00:20:28,830 --> 00:20:30,200
Your Wonder Doc

447
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:32,070
even saved that patient

448
00:20:32,070 --> 00:20:33,550
whose brain was spilling out

449
00:20:33,550 --> 00:20:34,750
at the hospital.

450
00:20:35,350 --> 00:20:36,240
I bet

451
00:20:36,270 --> 00:20:38,070
as long as he's at Xiaoximen Hospital,

452
00:20:38,070 --> 00:20:38,720
our business

453
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:40,650
will keep getting worse and worse.

454
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:42,200
Chen.

455
00:20:44,720 --> 00:20:45,440
Chen.

456
00:20:46,960 --> 00:20:47,960
You're hopeless.

457
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:05,000
You can drink with everyone else,

458
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:05,860
but not with me?

459
00:21:05,920 --> 00:21:06,830
Fill it up. Come on.

460
00:21:06,830 --> 00:21:08,480
Zhong, Zhong.

461
00:21:09,200 --> 00:21:10,830
How much weight have you gained?

462
00:21:10,830 --> 00:21:12,760
Huang, this liquor's pretty good.

463
00:21:14,270 --> 00:21:15,510
Huang's treating us!

464
00:21:15,510 --> 00:21:16,640
Look at this spread!

465
00:21:16,920 --> 00:21:18,920
It's fine to mix these two.

466
00:21:20,160 --> 00:21:21,560
We'll mix them together.

467
00:21:23,590 --> 00:21:24,350
Hold on,

468
00:21:24,350 --> 00:21:26,110
the rest of the dishes aren't out yet.

469
00:21:26,110 --> 00:21:27,440
Here come the cold dishes!

470
00:21:27,440 --> 00:21:27,960
Have you gained weight?

471
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:28,510
Yeah.

472
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:30,650
I could tell just by looking at you.

473
00:21:30,790 --> 00:21:31,440
Huang,

474
00:21:31,440 --> 00:21:33,030
look at you, even combing your hair!

475
00:21:33,030 --> 00:21:33,590
What's

476
00:21:33,590 --> 00:21:34,440
the occasion? Got some good news or what?

477
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:36,040
It's just from wearing a hat.

478
00:21:36,110 --> 00:21:37,400
No, wait till tomorrow,

479
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:38,110
when I do my runway walk.

480
00:21:38,110 --> 00:21:39,840
I'll tell you all about it then.

481
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:41,830
All right, you guys eat first.

482
00:21:41,830 --> 00:21:43,490
I'll bring out the hot dishes.

483
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:45,260
Come on, everyone.

484
00:21:45,720 --> 00:21:46,550
W-What?

485
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:48,030
S-Should I start us off with a toast?

486
00:21:48,030 --> 00:21:48,590
Go ahead.

487
00:21:49,160 --> 00:21:49,830
Come on, come on.

488
00:21:49,830 --> 00:21:51,350
I'm the senior one here, right?

489
00:21:51,350 --> 00:21:51,680
Exactly.

490
00:21:51,680 --> 00:21:53,200
All right, I'll make the toast.

491
00:21:53,200 --> 00:21:54,310
Well,

492
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:57,400
there are two things I want to say today.

493
00:21:57,790 --> 00:21:59,240
Just Two things,

494
00:21:59,240 --> 00:21:59,640
only two.

495
00:21:59,640 --> 00:22:00,510
First,

496
00:22:00,750 --> 00:22:02,720
we're here to celebrate

497
00:22:03,310 --> 00:22:04,960
Dr. Liu's triumphant arrival

498
00:22:04,960 --> 00:22:06,750
at Xiaoximen Hospital.

499
00:22:07,240 --> 00:22:08,070
A round of applause!

500
00:22:08,070 --> 00:22:09,730
A triumphant arrival indeed!

501
00:22:10,030 --> 00:22:11,240
And s-second,

502
00:22:11,590 --> 00:22:12,350
what's the second thing?

503
00:22:12,350 --> 00:22:13,410
We're celebrating

504
00:22:13,640 --> 00:22:14,640
our hospital's success

505
00:22:14,640 --> 00:22:15,880
in performing Zhang Jiao's surgery.

506
00:22:15,880 --> 00:22:16,880
In all these years,

507
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:18,160
we've never had such an...

508
00:22:18,160 --> 00:22:20,350
such an outstanding achievement.

509
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:22,480
This is a big deal.

510
00:22:23,310 --> 00:22:24,590
From now on,

511
00:22:24,590 --> 00:22:25,790
we're all one family,

512
00:22:25,830 --> 00:22:27,630
so we should help each other out.

513
00:22:28,160 --> 00:22:29,680
So this toast is really

514
00:22:29,680 --> 00:22:31,270
for today's guest of honor,

515
00:22:32,240 --> 00:22:33,110
Dr. Liu—

516
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:34,800
our very own Liu Zhengliang!

517
00:22:35,680 --> 00:22:37,680
May you weather every storm ahead

518
00:22:37,880 --> 00:22:40,080
and face life's hardships with a smile.

519
00:22:42,480 --> 00:22:43,540
-Cheers.
-Come on.

520
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:44,750
-Cheers.
-Come on.

521
00:22:44,750 --> 00:22:45,240
-Cheers.
-Come on.

522
00:22:45,240 --> 00:22:46,480
Let's have a few drinks.

523
00:22:46,480 --> 00:22:47,310
Pretty good,

524
00:22:47,310 --> 00:22:47,920
right?

525
00:22:47,920 --> 00:22:48,750
Come on.

526
00:22:49,920 --> 00:22:51,180
It tastes really sour.

527
00:22:51,550 --> 00:22:53,030
Here come the hot dishes!

528
00:22:54,750 --> 00:22:55,410
How's that?

529
00:22:55,790 --> 00:22:56,920
Quite a spread, huh?

530
00:22:58,960 --> 00:22:59,400
What do you think?

531
00:22:59,400 --> 00:23:00,350
Yeah, yeah, looks great!

532
00:23:00,350 --> 00:23:01,070
Dr. Liu,

533
00:23:01,310 --> 00:23:02,960
I've heard all about what you've done.

534
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:03,880
You're amazing!

535
00:23:03,880 --> 00:23:05,720
These two dishes are
on the house, just for you.

536
00:23:05,720 --> 00:23:06,720
Sweet and sour pork
and braised pork bones.

537
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:07,380
How's that?

538
00:23:07,790 --> 00:23:09,270
These are way too generous.

539
00:23:09,270 --> 00:23:10,240
You bet!

540
00:23:10,270 --> 00:23:11,640
N-No, it's not necessary.

541
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:12,240
Thank you.

542
00:23:12,720 --> 00:23:13,680
What's this?

543
00:23:13,790 --> 00:23:15,720
Getting all formal with me today?

544
00:23:16,350 --> 00:23:17,550
It's just that I don't like

545
00:23:17,550 --> 00:23:19,150
taking advantage of people.

546
00:23:19,830 --> 00:23:21,350
How's that taking advantage of anyone?

547
00:23:21,350 --> 00:23:22,030
We all help

548
00:23:22,030 --> 00:23:23,720
each other out, right?

549
00:23:24,160 --> 00:23:25,310
If I ever get sick,

550
00:23:25,310 --> 00:23:26,480
I'll come see you at the hospital.

551
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:27,350
You'd give me

552
00:23:27,350 --> 00:23:29,920
a couple extra bottles of glucose,
wouldn't you?

553
00:23:29,920 --> 00:23:30,440
Um,

554
00:23:30,440 --> 00:23:32,000
hospital rules won't let me

555
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:33,070
give you glucose for free.

556
00:23:33,070 --> 00:23:33,680
And I won't eat a single bite

557
00:23:33,680 --> 00:23:35,070
of these two dishes.

558
00:23:36,030 --> 00:23:37,510
The boss lady's just joking with you.

559
00:23:37,510 --> 00:23:38,880
You think she'd really

560
00:23:38,880 --> 00:23:39,750
ask you for glucose?

561
00:23:39,750 --> 00:23:40,440
If she ever does—

562
00:23:40,440 --> 00:23:41,640
look, if she asks you for any,

563
00:23:41,640 --> 00:23:42,110
j-just tell me.

564
00:23:42,110 --> 00:23:43,240
I'll get it for her.

565
00:23:43,350 --> 00:23:44,920
I-It's only a couple of bottles, right?

566
00:23:44,920 --> 00:23:45,680
Huang,

567
00:23:45,680 --> 00:23:46,920
if you're getting them for me,

568
00:23:46,920 --> 00:23:49,120
I'll have to ask for a few extra bottles!

569
00:23:49,440 --> 00:23:50,370
Come on, you two!

570
00:23:50,680 --> 00:23:51,550
With you two being so close,

571
00:23:51,550 --> 00:23:53,010
you don't even need to ask!

572
00:23:53,240 --> 00:23:54,510
All right, enjoy.

573
00:23:54,790 --> 00:23:55,720
Come on, come on.

574
00:23:56,160 --> 00:23:57,590
Dig in! Try the sweet and sour pork.

575
00:23:57,590 --> 00:23:58,110
Come on.

576
00:23:58,110 --> 00:23:59,790
This sweet and sour pork is excellent!

577
00:23:59,790 --> 00:24:00,680
Come on, let's have a toast.

578
